                        "review": "You ask yourself, why play this game when BlazBlue Centralfiction exists and is being updated again? Chronophantasma has worse online and less characters than the latest game. Why bother? I will tell you the two very valid reasons I'll gladly recommend this: \n\n1. Much better, varied and challenging Single-player content.\n2. English Dub voice acting.\n\nCentralfiction removed and changed single-player modes making it a worse single-player experience. To that game's credit they did improve the base Arcade Mode slightly, but not enough to compensate for the removal of the previous modes.\n\nFor one, they removed the most challenging mode in the series: Unlimited Mars. This game has selectable Boss variations of every character that you can use, and when the CPU uses them it has a superior AI to even max Hell difficulty. Unlimited Mars is a boss rush mode against these Bosses that is EXTREMELY challenging to even pro gamers. If you are someone who likes a single-player challenge then this is the best one.\n\nSecond, they changed Abyss mode (dungeon mode) in Centralfiction from this game. It might be a matter of taste which one you prefer, but I prefer Chronophantasmas. They added a boss rush at the end of Centralfictions, but it's not remotely the same as Unlimited Mars, and Chronophantasma has you meet bosses too in Abyss Mode, which you face with your upgrades, stats and special abilities for that mode. Not to mention it has Infinite Mode here where you can just fight forever if you chose to do so while enemies keep getting stronger and stronger.\n\nThird, it has Highlander Mode where you face up against a big bad final boss with any characters you like.\n\nLastly, the game has more story content not in Centralfiction in the form of a visual novel \"Remix Heart Gaiden\" which is an adaptation of the manga with that very name featuring Mai Natsume's own story. It also has a mode called \"Teach Me More, Miss Litchi!\" which is a comedic skit classroom refresher of all of the BlazBlue story so far for those who want to understand the lore.\n\nTo end, I'll just comment on the English Dub which is not present in Centralfiction. It's great, I love it. Hilarious at times, and even if I always used japanese in Centralfiction I find myself amused by understanding everything they say while fighting and there are plenty of fun lines. Recommended.\n\nIf these things sound interesting to you, know that it's probably worth getting as the gameplay itself is not much of a stepdown from Centralfiction. In fact, it's the same engine and I feel like it's almost the same. You are sacrificing online for these perks, but you can always just play Centralfiction for the online and this for the singleplayer.\n\nEnjoy!",
